"Predicate adjectives and participles"}, {"id": "a7a7d892-b25c-4d15-8f2a-c8b51ed45411", "type": "concept", "title": "Prepositional government and regime"}], "description": "Agreement is treated as a system of relationships, not a set of isolated corrections."}, {"id": "6d6c1d59-dd5e-402d-b6ed-1168e4a9a4d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Word order and emphasis", "children": [{"id": "a30316f3-b338-46a8-8b4d-993177f8b00e", "type": "concept", "title": "Canonical SVO order"}, {"id": "8ad33efe-b902-4f37-aaf4-50893c3190b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Fronting for emphasis"}, {"id": "116c10b7-1a55-4c58-ad6e-b698db211517", "type": "concept", "title": "Postverbal subjects"}, {"id": "71a61671-2267-45b6-8222-76fb2d3658cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Placement of modifiers and adverbs"}], "description": "Students practice how Spanish uses position to manage emphasis, topic, focus, and natural flow."}]}, {"id": "8cd55276-12f1-4eaa-b358-7ba3770a04b3", "type": "topic", "title": "Mood, Modality, and Subjunctive Choice", "description": "The subjunctive becomes a tool for meaning: uncertainty, evaluation, influence, anticipation, and stance. Students learn when mood choice changes what a sentence claims.", "children": [{"id": "c6ae1f8d-0b72-4ddc-a48b-6754f51718cc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Noun clauses", "children": [{"id": "158feed4-689c-4828-a5a2-b7d66aaa2882", "type": "concept", "title": "Wishes and influence"}, {"id": "e6b0fd20-e605-4d10-b306-ffc59fba1c8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Doubt, denial, and probability"}, {"id": "693eb72d-da18-4aea-a160-bdcb184d1d56", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotion and evaluation"}, {"id": "234d8ebe-52a6-44b9-97db-91e4b18498d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicative after assertion and certainty"}], "description": "Students connect mood selection to verbs of desire, doubt, emotion, denial, recommendation, and perception."}, {"id": "eb14ca4c-44ad-490d-954f-7b39c04cda8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adjective clauses", "children": [