ept", "title": "Progressive constructions"}], "description": "Students refine contrasts among completed action, background description, habitual action, and ongoing states."}, {"id": "d491ceca-b186-4bf4-b829-e530a60f03c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sequence of tenses", "children": [{"id": "6d14ffba-a085-41a7-bfdc-dfac02a99974", "type": "concept", "title": "Present-triggered subjunctive"}, {"id": "548c2736-3c79-4399-a28b-3443e72f6c52", "type": "concept", "title": "Past-triggered subjunctive"}, {"id": "73b1a994-4270-43ef-8d6a-1fcb1d2decdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditional and future perspectives"}, {"id": "e366d6ed-725a-470d-9add-e9ac1ecb9d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Reported speech"}], "description": "Students learn how main-clause tense constrains subordinate-clause tense in formal and academic contexts."}, {"id": "04763ef9-ae3d-4786-a80d-9c63953b23db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hypothesis and counterfactuality", "children": [{"id": "56f01609-1f2e-4dd5-a6d7-a87eeba27eac", "type": "concept", "title": "Si clauses"}, {"id": "cbab802a-5fef-464e-9b60-7814667e5a12", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditional perfect"}, {"id": "83526c3d-5060-413b-8635-f36cbe31c751", "type": "concept", "title": "Pluperfect subjunctive"}, {"id": "0e734c58-2506-4de3-89f0-09a418c7f068", "type": "concept", "title": "Modal verbs and probability"}], "description": "Students practice the grammar of possible, improbable, and unreal situations."}]}, {"id": "0adc3c2c-d134-49fd-b483-305e3dc38067", "type": "topic", "title": "Pronouns, Clitics, and Reference", "description": "This unit targets the small words that carry a large burden in Spanish: object pronouns, clitics, demonstratives, possessives, and reference chains.", "children": [{"id": "6894a4c6-8582-49a4-b929-74c2112db5c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Object pronouns", "children": [{"id": "29fcd8ca-2265-4c76-b483-442906041c9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct and indirect objects"}, {"id": "6364624d-fde8-4281-84a4-dd1