 learn to expand, compress, and vary sentence structure without losing clarity. The goal is syntactic maturity, not long sentences for their own sake.", "children": [{"id": "98d562df-4e2d-4309-96ae-46444400aac4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relative clauses", "children": [{"id": "cf954fce-3f41-44fe-9bac-d3e0153ab656", "type": "concept", "title": "Que, quien, cual, cuyo"}, {"id": "de1071be-3760-4fed-a97c-35e4e296aacc", "type": "concept", "title": "Restrictive and nonrestrictive clauses"}, {"id": "3edf6d93-4ef7-468e-846e-86253c3dcb14", "type": "concept", "title": "Preposition + relative pronoun"}, {"id": "22b1e0d1-fed6-4fa5-a43b-b4dbdc0ac860", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative clauses in academic definitions"}], "description": "Students use relative clauses to add precision while controlling agreement, prepositions, and register."}, {"id": "ca179d69-6895-4992-9d6d-2715cb8b7495", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nominalizations and infinitive clauses", "children": [{"id": "3a843f73-deb3-4eb9-aced-66cee5ca4db9", "type": "concept", "title": "Infinitive clauses"}, {"id": "b5e59c1f-a9fb-4685-bc63-d5915ed68705", "type": "concept", "title": "Gerund cautions"}, {"id": "8ab75ee0-c22a-41bd-9e24-34eecfd49a42", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominalized actions"}, {"id": "38d32697-5de5-4b55-bb6c-76e438c84bae", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding over-nominalization"}], "description": "Students practice compact academic style and alternatives to repeated subordinate clauses."}, {"id": "fda88413-968c-4683-a225-336ac1cd2e7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sentence combining for style", "children": [{"id": "50a25c7a-1db3-49d7-8b51-7273551bfdff", "type": "concept", "title": "Combining short sentences"}, {"id": "cad0dcbd-b333-4c50-acbe-d5e59ccc58c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Breaking overloaded sentences"}, {"id": "0f9ae3f4-b0f7-436f-97e5-4a354b428d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Parallel structure"}, {"id": "e3e5cbff-a65a-419a-ac24-318dfbf9cf84", "type": "concept", "title": "Punctuation with embedded clauses"}], "description": "Revision workshops focus on sentence variety, logic, and rhythm."}]}, {"id": "fd30d56e-257f-4d34-894e-bd57d6cd9379", "type": "topic", "title": "Cohesion, Discourse Connectors, and Information Structure", "description": "This unit shifts from sentence-level correctness to paragraph-level movement. Students learn how Spanish academic prose signals sequence, contrast, cause, concession, and emphasis.", "children": [{"id": "b9ad88c0-02ce-4281-8d51-c2375629d4dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Connectors and logical relations", "children": [{"id": "c0bbcd25-3952-4702-8f25-8e482ca1aa34", "type": "concept", "title": "Addition and sequence"}, {"id": "b63bb95c-3a53-4bf5-b29f-2f6b6de8e6d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Cause and result"}, {"id": "63425f7c-6c5b-48e5-853d-a9ebc1201cc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and concession"}, {"id": "dc846c1e-ba7a-496d-9e01-b8d89a59982c", "type": "concept", "title": "Reformulation and conclusion"}], "description": "Students build a flexible connector repertoire and learn the grammar that follows each connector."}, {"id": "8c9ba84d-446f-4916-8d3b-2b272bcad31e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theme-rheme progression", "children": [{"id": "ad1787c6-42ed-4562-a667-b112100ac6f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Topic sentences in Spanish"}, {"id": "4b1ec9b1-b0bd-4031-96cb-80073f1408ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Given-new information flow"}, {"id": "559aac35-ba97-4f57-8177-61f46ab28562", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions between paragraphs"}, {"id": "6439aa35-73d7-447b-9fde-c830a788dc92", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding abrupt shifts"}], "description": "Students learn to manage old and new information so paragraphs feel coherent."}, {"id": "d982e111-093a-41b8-abfe-6b3af4dceba8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cohesive devices", "children": [{"id": "ccdc489c-a262-488e-859c-825a7a107278", "type": "concept", "title": "Lexical chains"}, {"id": "315f6f76-1639-40f4-9a06-dee1812e13f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Synonymy and reformulation"}, {"id": "cf9f5995-7dd6-4170-9f42-495e39a06775", "type": "concept", "title": "Pronoun reference"}, {"id": "695c001c-1fa5-4d15-a8e2-7a4de15eb5e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ellipsis and repetition control"}], "description": "Students practice lexical and grammatical cohesion beyond repeated connector phrases."}]}, {"id": "2bbe65ff-f452-4b95-a8ae-1910eef01d24", "type": "topic", "title": "Register, Style, and Academic Tone", "description": "Students learn to choose language appropriate to audience, genre, and purpose: formal essays, critiques, presentations, correspondence, and culturally situated argument.", "children": [{"id": "908789c9-ed85-4b7a-bc00-f0352e5d3f87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Register control", "children": [{"id": "d2e4a608-a94a-4cfa-b927-fa2fdf88adce", "type": "concept", "title": "Tuteo and usted"}, {"id": "c19765ae-b345-4660-af06-f6d79805422b", "type": "concept", "title": "Colloquial versus formal vocabulary"}, {"id": "ec53bf12-242b-419b-9c5a-43e890116ebd", "type": "concept", "title": "Formulaic academic expressions"}, {"id": "26db1200-439f-43bd-8f81-b89e34dd8f2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding anglicized register"}], "description": "Students distinguish informal, neutral, formal, and academic options."}, {"id": "0256555c-75f2-410c-850d-a73ba986167c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Style and voice", "children": [{"id": "8a56e4e0-9a91-4097-9a39-7a0332ee2e2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Conciseness"}, {"id": "a94cd250-0b17-45e5-9977-fcfdaea15fb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Emphasis"}, {"id": "1a1d137b-0831-4f2f-81fa-36e55d0f215d", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal versus verbal style"}, {"id": "709af549-cae0-484b-83c4-470510532255", "type": "concept", "title": "Sentence rhythm"}], "description": "Students develop a precise, economical style that still sounds natural in Spanish."}, {"id": "8c72083f-38db-445e-b7e8-6256ae411369", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genre conventions", "children": [{"id": "55b370a8-1c8a-4329-970b-04eab719b83a", "type": "concept", "title": "Analytical paragraph"}, {"id": "28daa406-1090-401f-9ef0-a41308c6587e", "type": "concept", "title": "Literary or cultural commentary"}, {"id": "b9360499-0eb6-436e-b8b7-38ad7e9e8ac8", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic email and proposal"}, {"id": "da184ce5-218d-4344-ac0d-545051a850a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Oral presentation handout"}], "description": "Students learn the expectations of common advanced undergraduate writing tasks."}]}, {"id": "03cebdd7-377b-4f57-9471-dc2e3e113f73", "type": "topic", "title": "Lexical Precision, Collocation, and Idiomaticity", "description": "World-class composition depends on vocabulary control at the phrase level. This unit trains students to choose words that fit meaning, register, region, and collocation.", "children": [{"id": "d29e686d-da1e-4ba4-9087-c4c27cf68db4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lexical selection", "children": [{"id": "45770cf6-f680-4689-8120-985daf0fa041", "type": "concept", "title": "False cognates"}, {"id": "5cc0bf51-df95-4f8d-a9d9-589d62eceae6", "type": "concept", "title": "Polysemy"}, {"id": "7708cb05-9975-475e-9e1b-9e39dec894a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Semantic fields"}, {"id": "425c4983-9bdd-452e-b068-3e0f387e2fa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic verbs of analysis"}], "description": "Students move beyond dictionary equivalence into context-sensitive word choice."}, {"id": "bb2073b2-74e6-4e5e-94d5-7f997ec25b71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collocations and phraseology", "children": [{"id": "1d81892a-f2b9-471c-aab8-79efc3410a41", "type": "concept", "title": "Verb-noun collocations"}, {"id": "aba6640a-8c2e-4b9e-9f40-0ac85fe2bd76", "type": "concept", "title": "Adjective-noun collocations"}, {"id": "2ae1f3fe-fea9-48fb-8051-d5627533878d", "type": "concept", "title": "Prepositional phrases"}, {"id": "4d2a179d-104f-41eb-a21b-bd6dec0a2745", "type": "concept", "title": "Set academic expressions"}], "description": "Students learn which words naturally occur together in educated Spanish."}, {"id": "60301bf7-57c6-467e-a08d-7b469ed95cbf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corpus-informed revision", "children": [{"id": "e57d9ed3-6712-4030-891c-c31d5785b11b", "type": "concept", "title": "RAE and ASALE resources"}, {"id": "467607c8-01e5-4915-af09-291c18a3e7ef", "type": "concept", "title": "CORPES and CREA-style searches"}, {"id": "9cc0b518-7f9d-41de-9ef0-60af5534c60a", "type": "concept", "title": "Frequency and register awareness"}, {"id": "174b5263-998a-4093-8138-f8a8967529f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting usage choices"}], "description": "Students use dictionaries, corpora, and authoritative usage sources to test hypotheses about usage."}]}, {"id": "7db8dee8-98de-40a0-8265-497c67983614", "type": "topic", "title": "Orthography, Accentuation, and Punctuation", "description": "Advanced writing requires command of the visible system of Spanish: accents, capitalization, punctuation, quotation conventions, and proofreading standards.", "children": [{"id": "e1f083c4-75fc-4bb6-9ad4-72984b23fb8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accentuation and spelling", "children": [{"id": "1bdbcc89-6443-442a-a2ed-eb91ed226d96", "type": "concept", "title": "Tilde rules"}, {"id": "e152182f-8813-4190-bfab-033459ea7147", "type": "concept", "title": "Diacritical accents"}, {"id": "180c7239-7dd5-48a4-a4ab-dccb2b227a59", "type": "concept", "title": "Hiatus and diphthongs"}, {"id": "78a4294b-6af3-46ae-932d-78e9f129a78c", "type": "concept", "title": "Common spelling traps"}], "description": "Students review rules that frequently affect upper-level writing accuracy."}, {"id": "47a75f9c-c811-428a-8d16-0a8f9a9d2b2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Punctuation in complex prose", "children": [{"id": "9ae776e2-808c-443e-ae07-ed81ab0719e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Comma with subordinate clauses"}, {"id": "161a293b-f415-4164-ae5e-3c4b34c25ffd", "type": "concept", "title": "Semicolons and colons"}, {"id": "e05c9bce-dee2-49a3-94a9-114f49af74fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Parentheses and dashes"}, {"id": "39c91eca-56e5-4866-90bf-9c31ec2ece6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Quotation punctuation"}], "description": "Students learn punctuation as a meaning-making tool, especially in subordinated and analytical prose."}, {"id": "749e0b34-e614-4a27-9dee-696f78c218f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Normative reference habits", "children": [{"id": "d2a9ab8c-3401-4444-a171-13de2f442a5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Diccionario panhispanico de dudas"}, {"id": "37be8cbc-92de-4c73-90e7-af1723041dd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Ortografia de la lengua espanola"}, {"id": "e6c82632-780f-492e-9d70-b94b0f5381fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Fundeu recommendations"}, {"id": "abeb3986-fba9-45cb-9971-191383317bdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency across a manuscript"}], "description": "Students practice consulting authoritative resources when editing disputed forms."}]}, {"id": "177d659d-d729-4563-974d-b1cfe3d5375e", "type": "topic", "title": "Summary, Critique, and Argumentation", "description": "Students use grammar and style in meaningful intellectual tasks: summarizing accurately, evaluating claims, and constructing persuasive arguments in Spanish.", "children": [{"id": "6aecd9d0-c4ba-47f4-b2bb-5197f72bdf7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Academic summary", "children": [{"id": "518fe4bb-5ee8-4b40-a202-1af163087fd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Main claim identification"}, {"id": "33692dd1-1743-40f3-83c8-ac527ce39854", "type": "concept", "title": "Paraphrase"}, {"id": "284e878a-3221-477e-9408-9062d8261617", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribution verbs"}, {"id": "6ba88559-283d-47fa-9c47-afd5f7270ffe", "type": "concept", "title": "Neutral stance"}], "description": "Students learn to compress a text without copying its structure or losing its logic."}, {"id": "3ef7cd0a-4216-480e-9a00-e0dcf12bb6b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical response", "chil